se rows are given by $a,$ $b,$ and $c.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{aligned}|-(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}|+2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(0\\cdot 2-4\\cdot 3)+(2\\cdot 2-2\\cdot 3)+2(2\\cdot 4-2\\cdot 0) \\\\  & =-12-2+16 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299583 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "771cc149-2f2f-5147-82d6-b25bff5aa208" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298071}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "771cc149-2f2f-5147-82d6-b25bff5aa208" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298071} :answer-field/id #uuid "c69c83b4-8ce3-5770-b7b0-9b88367956e6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299304}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e7f80b43-a2f5-515b-92f2-1141b2bd6cfe" :question/math-academy-id "q-317312" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨2,-1,3⟩$, $b=⟨0,4,1⟩$ and $c=⟨-2,1,5⟩.$ Find $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ using a determinant.\n\n$a\\cdot (b\\times c)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the scalar triple product $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ is just the determinant of the matrix whose rows are given by $a,$ $b,$ and $c.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}|\\,-\\,(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{aligned}|\\,+\\,3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\,(4\\cdot 5-1\\cdot 1)\\,-\\,(-1)\\,(0\\cdot 5-1\\cdot (-2))\\,+\\,3\\,(0\\cdot 1-4\\cdot (-2)) \\\\