 \\operatorname{sin}⁡{11}^{∘} \\\\  & =286\\cdot (0.190\\,809) \\\\  & ≈54.57,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to two decimal places."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295109 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f78eeff4-6664-5afb-aa43-f6574f9a819d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10.3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293897}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f78eeff4-6664-5afb-aa43-f6574f9a819d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10.3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293897} :answer-field/id #uuid "52057c52-87e1-53a7-8ea5-eae346dfaaf1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294223}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "932a647f-64da-5961-9b0d-b120fe29bcc3" :question/math-academy-id "q-279752" :question/problem "![](images/f4/f41ad0635fb7bb426a387f825097a31dddb591861012f2543336a142832df9db.png)\n\nRounded to the **nearest tenth**, the area of $△ABC$ above is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}ac\\operatorname{sin}⁡B,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠B$ is between the sides of lengths $a$ and $b.$ \n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =AB=4, \\\\ a & =BC=8, \\\\ m∠B & ={40}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡{40}^{∘}=0.642\\,788,\n$$\n\nrounded to six decimal places,  we calculate the area as follows:\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 8\\cdot 4\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{40}^{∘} \\\\  & =16\\cdot (0.642\\,788) \\\\  & ≈10.3,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the **nearest tenth**."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295110 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b2e420a9-a7bd-5017-809e-98b732958447" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "93.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293632}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b2e420a9-a7bd-5017-809e-98b732958447" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "93.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293632} :answer-field/id #uuid "d61c4e2c-bb73-58b5-9e0a-477efb52fb86" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294685}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e614497f-203d-5c49-a415-3fb541b41cc1" :question/math-academy-id "q-279753" :question/problem "![](images/68/68977537a5f180dd483534ed1415326251d4a76a3dd0833e9701487cd8b5b33d.png)\n\nRounded to the **nearest tenth**, the area of $△ABC$ is{{field-1}} ${\\text{ft}}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}bc\\operatorname{sin}⁡A,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠A$ is between the sides of lengths $b$ and $c.$ \n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}с & =AB=18, \\\\ b & =AC=12, \\\\ m∠A & ={120}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡{120}^{∘}=0.866\\,025,\n$$\n\nrounded to six decimal places,  we calculate the area as follows:\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 12\\cdot 18\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{120}^{∘} \\\\  & =108\\cdot (0.866\\,025…) \\\\  & ≈93.5\\,{\\text{ft}}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the **nearest tenth**."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295123 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7e971691-e630-503f-870f-b92b3ea2ce77" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10.83" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293443}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7e971691-e630-503f-870f-b92b3ea2ce77" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10.83" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293443} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f6faf19-04cc-502f-9255-547f6f88a2b3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294377}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8878e119-056d-550e-93df-4c14bd85326c" :question/math-academy-id "q-280260" :question/problem "![](images/20/200dcd87827ae9683ba0ecb3b284509b31d32f9e0dc1b9736a260d2f7d71b0a0.png)\n\nRounded to **two decimal places**, the area of $△ABC$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}ac\\operatorname{sin}⁡B,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠B$ is between the sides of lengths $a$ and $c.$ \n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =AB=5, \\\\ a & =BC=5, \\\\ m∠B & ={60}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘}=0.866\\,025,\n$$\n\nrounded to six decimal places,  we calculate the area as follows:\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 5\\cdot 5\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘} \\\\  & =12.5\\cdot (0.866\\,025) \\\\  & ≈10.83,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to **two decimal places**."}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of a Triangle"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105904 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105579 :question/id #uuid "c8d31ea4-41c6-5f24-bf7a-a950a30342d7" :question/math-academy-id "e-4253" :question/problem "The area of ​​the triangle $\\triangle ABC$ is $24\\sqrt{2} \\text{ cm}^2.$ Find $AB.$\n\n![](images/e9/e93e732bd04cfda304c2098087548a638d8d869ccf8b1050235e8207825875d3.png)" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\n\\mathcal{A}=\\dfrac{1}{2}bc\\sin{A},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\angle{A}$ is between the sides of lengths $b$ and $c.$ \n\nHere\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =AB, \\\\ b & =AC=12\\text{ cm}, \\\\ m∠A & ={45}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince \n\n$$\n\\sin{45^{\\circ}} = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},\n$$\n\nwe can calculate $c=AB,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot c\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ 24\\sqrt{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 12\\cdot c\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{45}^{∘} \\\\ 24\\sqrt{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 12\\cdot c\\cdot (\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}) \\\\ 24\\cancel{\\sqrt{2}} & =3\\cancel{\\sqrt{2}}c \\\\ 24 & =3c \\\\ c & =8\\text{ cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that $AB = 8\\,\\textrm{cm}.$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cafdb077-0e02-5e7a-bf78-c3a8aacfb6f7" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106346 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "82c2824d-4c33-5f10-819c-b4fe7eba4b17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10cm" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104225} {:answer/id #uuid "982a032b-da28-51db-adfe-d8dc2bae6084" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{25}{2}cm" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104226} {:answer/id #uuid "d9d54c45-2e87-572c-9614-1942d00976fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9cm" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104227} {:answer/id #uuid "fe4e80a5-5971-53b2-996a-1eb617121c09" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7cm" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104228} {:answer/id #uuid "57c30440-beed-5e2a-b00e-75b39f949444" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{22}{3}cm" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104229}] :answer-field/id #uuid "04104815-55f0-5585-b546-93a2c497895f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104224}] :question/id #uuid "e987c676-ae94-5f92-bdbb-ee11dc914f54" :question/math-academy-id "q-43310" :question/problem "![](images/cc/cce0e775722bbaaa8eeeb60a7cd097e8ad59b7c83c838f072416112aed657e33.png)\n\nThe area of ​​the triangle $△ABC$ is $\\frac{21}{4}cm^{2}$. Find $AC$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106347 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a1135cf5-2a63-566c-bd0c-129c84f6e24a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "65^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104231} {:answer/id #uuid "c5e48878-b541-5b26-aae6-4283b0d479cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "50^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104232} {:answer/id #uuid "139637a3-5b2a-566b-8168-d2af651ada8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "75^{∘}" :db/id #e