{:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277870}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1a46e83d-b704-567c-8d00-1886b9f6bc9b" :question/math-academy-id "q-161107" :question/problem "![](images/ef/ef8379b21526455a723369fda4360e2d7d3ef3cf54ce7d7767df7bd160a169f4.png)\n\nThe area of ​​the triangle $△ABC$ is $5\\sqrt{3}\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.$ Find $AC.$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}bc\\operatorname{sin}⁡A,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠A$ is between the sides of lengths $b$ and $c.$ \n\nHere\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =AB=5\\text{ cm}, \\\\ b & =AC, \\\\ m∠A & ={60}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘}=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},\n$$\n\nwe can calculate $b=AC,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot c\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ 5\\sqrt{3} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot 5\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘} \\\\ 5\\sqrt{3} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot 5\\cdot (\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}) \\\\ 5\\sqrt{3} & =\\frac{5\\sqrt{3}\\,b}{4} \\\\ \\cancel{5\\sqrt{3}} & =\\frac{\\cancel{5\\sqrt{3}}\\,b}{4} \\\\ 1 & =\\frac{b}{4} \\\\ b & =4\\text{ cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that $AC=4\\,\\text{cm}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278383 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a92871f-5bd5-581e-ac06-dbd13021c053" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275724} {:answer/id #uuid "299f96e2-93fa-5d8f-ab41-fc313dbd3222" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7.5\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275854} {:answer/id #uuid "4f831c2c-96bc-514e-94a8-9c7ae9a2e9a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276188} {:answer/id #uuid "7bb62d91-e7c1-5a0b-9594-0da656f39663" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6.5\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276601} {:answer/id #uuid "a89eff61-0284-58bc-8453-86df1e739eb6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276998}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1a92871f-5bd5-581e-ac06-dbd13021c053" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275724} :answer-field/id #uuid "e821e218-a2a4-5efe-86d2-0f9a4556c28f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278132}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "43fd23a0-08b8-58ee-b7e6-43240cfa05d7" :question/math-academy-id "q-161109" :question/problem "![](images/b9/b95571772af958b4f7b7dcdbba630b78e029c838340dc272809a6c7915dc9c90.png)\n\nThe area of ​​the triangle $△ABC$ is $\\frac{21\\sqrt{2}}{2}{\\text{ cm}}^{2}.$ Find $AC.$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}bc\\operatorname{sin}⁡A,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠A$ is between the sides of lengths $b$ and $c.$ \n\nHere\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =AB=6\\text{ cm}, \\\\ b & =AC, \\\\ m∠A & ={45}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡{45}^{∘}=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},\n$$\n\nwe can calculate $b=AC,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot c\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\frac{21\\sqrt{2}}{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot 6\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{45}^{∘} \\\\ \\frac{21\\sqrt{2}}{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot 6\\cdot (\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}) \\\\ \\frac{21\\sqrt{2}}{2} & =\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}\\,b}{2} \\\\ \\frac{21\\cancel{\\sqrt{2}}}{\\cancel{2}} & =\\frac{3\\cancel{\\sqrt{2}}\\,b}{\\cancel{2}} \\\\ 3b & =21 \\\\ b & =7\\text{ cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that $AC=7\\,\\text{cm}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295125 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6bc3b7ba-d476-5a69-8384-cf1fc304c535" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293380}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6bc3b7ba-d476-5a69-8384-cf1fc304c535" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293380} :answer-field/id #uuid "c798fd12-9751-5ada-a3f9-3336533400e9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294636}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "95d92df8-f5a2-5d44-90e8-e2bcbdb9b2d6" :question/math-academy-id "q-280279" :question/problem "![](images/86/866f869f43e2663c2f63a485049f84ae059e2fdcb73db0445eb355491957c66a.png)\n\nThe area of ​​the triangle $△ABC$ is $\\frac{25\\sqrt{3}}{2}{\\text{cm}}^{2}.$ Then,  $AC=${{field-1}} $\\text{cm}.$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}bc\\operatorname{sin}⁡A,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠A$ is between the sides of lengths $b$ and $c.$ \n\nHere\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =AB=10\\text{ cm}, \\\\ b & =AC, \\\\ m∠A & ={120}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡{120}^{∘}=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},\n$$\n\nwe can calculate $b=AC,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot c\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\frac{25\\sqrt{3}}{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot 10\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{120}^{∘} \\\\ \\frac{25\\sqrt{3}}{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot 10\\cdot (\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}) \\\\ \\frac{25\\sqrt{3}}{2} & =5b\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\ 25\\cancel{\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}} & =5b\\cdot \\cancel{\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}} \\\\ 5b & =25 \\\\ b & =5\\text{ cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that $AC=5\\,\\text{ cm}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295126 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bc7bcb4a-1dc3-5347-9368-68572b9b7d9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293664}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bc7bcb4a-1dc3-5347-9368-68572b9b7d9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293664} :answer-field/id #uuid "5521148e-fdbd-5362-a47a-ed6937115ac8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294231}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "13cfc4c2-60f9-5bce-a135-f2772aeb4d9b" :question/math-academy-id "q-280282" :question/problem "![](images/5c/5c0bf3060129e2a03dab0fcd2a6f0f6068d1ec565143b83d11ad4d8ae1b41b85.png)\n\nThe area of ​​the acute triangle $△ABC$ is $3{\\text{ mm}}^{2}.$ Then, the measure of $∠A$ is{{field-1}} ${}^{∘}.$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}bc\\operatorname{sin}⁡A,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠A$ is between the sides of lengths $b$ and $c.$ \n\nHere\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =AB=\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{ mm}, \\\\ b & =AC=4\\,\\text{mm}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $m∠A$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot c\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4\\cdot \\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ 3 & =2\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\frac{3}{2\\sqrt{3}} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡A & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\ m∠A & ={60}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323821 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2587a5f0-6774-56c5-ad31-19ae4ad1f0d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321439}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2587a5f0-6774-56c5-ad31-19ae4ad1f0d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321439} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a7cc960-d17f-5d6a-bfe0-389ce724bbce" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323382}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4332fa12-c2aa-5bc4-9e84-8c97ff265d0e" :question/math-academy-id "q-365424" :question/problem "![](images/7e/7ead42d83a971733b601f45dcc1ad545a52298fc8a800ba69344651a54f4830d.png)\n\nThe area of the acute triangle $△ABC$ is $20\\sqrt{2}{\\text{ cm}}^{2}.$ Then, the measure of $∠A$ is{{field-1}} ${}^{∘}.$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}bc\\operatorname{sin}⁡A,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠A$ is between the sides of lengths $b$ and $c.$ \n\nHere\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =AB=8\\,\\text{cm}, \\\\ b & =AC=10\\,\\text{cm}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $m∠A$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot c\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ 20\\sqrt{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 10\\cdot 8\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ 20\\sqrt{2} & =40\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\frac{20\\sqrt{2}}{40} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡A & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ m∠A & ={45}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329720 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00626454-06b5-5255-8b10-a969634f2a3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{40}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326940} {:answer/id #uuid "0a118cb1-bcf0-5192-ac99-50c6d218a0df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{50}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327022} {:answer/id #uuid "880cd774-4b0c-578b-9cb7-2a7f6ddc9ffe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{45}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328104} {:answer/id #uuid "9c24e516-7c4c-59ff-9120-8f3e8f967303" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{60}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328284} {:answer/id #uuid "e1eb75a8-96e9-5751-9380-e070f3e6a153" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{30}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328910}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "880cd774-4b0c-578b-9cb7-2a7f6ddc9ffe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{45}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328104} :answer-field/id #uuid "8cbb3be6-5963-5d28-9797-4fa8242fb4a9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329419}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8ffe80f4-577a-5763-8b79-42fa1192abfb" :question/math-academy-id "q-43328" :question/problem "![](images/f2/f2a9f5e6149b62b5724de8a46e50e7aac2976ffa2f9f841c64417ffd248fcb88.png)\n\nThe area of ​​the triangle $△ABC$ is $\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2}{\\text{ cm}}^{2}.$ Find the measure of $∠A.$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}bc\\operatorname{sin}⁡A,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠A$ is between the sides of lengths $b$ and $c.$ \n\nHere\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =AB=\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{ cm}, \\\\ b & =AC=\\sqrt{6}\\,\\text{cm}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $m∠A$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot c\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{6}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\cancel{\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2}} & =\\cancel{\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ 1 & =\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡A & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ m∠A & ={45}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329721 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "55cfe684-dc18-5ab1-b164-6d50fade618a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{45}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327676} {:answer/id #uuid "8d23ee9d-454e-5907-a98d-d759e11996ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{25}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328151} {:answer/id #uuid "b7359851-720e-5ab4-876a-6265d25f515d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{40}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328528} {:answer/id #uuid "cf531d87-8a79-5162-b024-e25dc07d7e53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{30}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328757} {:answer/id #uuid "e7164a97-e526-5ef2-8ced-7e38b414e248" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{35}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328954}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cf531d87-8a79-5162-b024-e25dc07d7e53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{30}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328757} :answer-field/id #uuid "fbc9b871-5875-5e5c-8a91-d0aec6bf5882" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329619}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "55d7cd50-6834-55b6-a52f-4f6d251b49dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-43339" :question/problem "![](images/85/85b13f2236c5f00da34ea71fdbfc967882fa6e66c347f6ef40c0604391a5d68e.png)\n\nThe area of ​​the triangle $△ABC$ is $15{\\text{ cm}}^{2}.$ Find $m∠A.$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}bc\\operatorname{sin}⁡A,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠A$ is between the sides of lengths $b$ and $c.$ \n\nHere\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =AB=5\\,\\text{ cm}, \\\\ b & =AC=12\\,\\text{cm}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $m∠A$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot c\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ 15 & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 12\\cdot 5\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ 15 & =30\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\frac{15}{30} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡A & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ m∠A & ={30}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating an Angle or Side of a Triangle Given the Area of a Triangle"}]}
